2.4Finite element function spaces
In the above discussion, we assumed that we could construct discrete subspaces Vh ⊂ V of infinitedimensional function spaces. A central aspect of the finite element method is the construction of such subspaces by patching together local function spaces defined by a set of finite elements. We here give a general overview of the construction of finite element function spaces and return in Chapters3and4 to the construction of specific function spaces as subsets of H1, H(curl), H(div) and L2.


